
<!-- 5c. Two lanes and four trend items (pass 2) -->
<section class="ss-sec" id="lanes" aria-labelledby="h-lanes">
  <header class="pm-section-head pm-section-head--page ss-head"><h2 id="h-lanes">Two lanes and four trend items</h2><span class="pm-meta">SPEC P.3 and P.4</span></header>
  <div class="ss-body">
    <p class="ss-lede">Pass 2 adds two ways in beside "describe your idea", each a first-class entry on the projects list and each with its own screens. The shell, the pins, the buttons and the tape anatomy are identical on every lane; only the words change (Ruling 14). Open <a href="flow.html">the flow prototype</a> and start from the projects list to walk both.</p>
    <div class="pm-table-scroll"><table class="pm-table ss-plain ss-wide"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Lane</th><th scope="col">Who it is for</th><th scope="col">The sentence, verbatim from the live build</th><th scope="col">Write rule, stated on its screens</th><th scope="col">Screens</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Describe your idea</strong><br><span class="pm-meta">Start a new product</span></td><td>The founder.</td><td>Describe your idea. Pramaan builds it, and you try it every sprint.</td><td>None: there is no existing code to write back to.</td><td><a href="screens/02-new-project.html">02</a> then 05b to 17</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Hand off your code</strong><br><span class="pm-meta">Lane A</span></td><td>A founder who already has code: an agency built it, a co-founder left, a no-code tool exported it. The same persona with one extra fear, that the original gets changed.</td><td>Upload it or import it from GitHub. Pramaan takes it from there, and you can take a copy back any time.</td><td>Pramaan never writes back to where the code came from.</td><td><a href="screens/18-handoff-source.html">18</a>, <a href="screens/18b-handoff-github.html">18b</a>, <a href="screens/18c-handoff-too-big.html">18c</a>, <a href="screens/18d-handoff-not-zip.html">18d</a>, <a href="screens/18e-handoff-github-permission.html">18e</a>, <a href="screens/19-handoff-copying.html">19</a>, <a href="screens/20-handoff-requirements.html">20</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Work in my repository</strong><br><span class="pm-meta">Lane B, "For engineering teams"</span></td><td>An engineering team member who owns a repository, reviews pull requests, merges and deploys. Plain, literal voice; not a founder.</td><td>Request features in a repository you own. Pramaan opens reviewed pull requests; you merge and deploy.</td><td>Pramaan never pushes to your default branch.</td><td><a href="screens/21-repo-connect.html">21</a>, <a href="screens/21b-repo-connect-permission.html">21b</a>, <a href="screens/21c-repo-connect-empty.html">21c</a>, <a href="screens/22-repo-requests.html">22</a>, <a href="screens/22b-repo-requests-empty.html">22b</a>, <a href="screens/23-repo-request.html">23</a>, <a href="screens/23b-repo-request-blocked.html">23b</a></td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <div class="ss-grid2">
      <div class="ss-card"><h3 class="pm-t-heading">Lane A, step by step</h3>
        <ol class="ss-list">
          <li><a href="screens/18-handoff-source.html">18</a> upload a .zip or import from GitHub; the copy-flow diagram follows the form.</li>
          <li>Failure states with one next action each: <a href="screens/18c-handoff-too-big.html">18c</a> too big, <a href="screens/18d-handoff-not-zip.html">18d</a> not a .zip, <a href="screens/18e-handoff-github-permission.html">18e</a> GitHub needs permission. <a href="screens/18b-handoff-github.html">18b</a> is the GitHub route.</li>
          <li><a href="screens/19-handoff-copying.html">19</a> the overview while the private copy is made: Working, locked destinations that still link.</li>
          <li><a href="screens/20-handoff-requirements.html">20</a> bring a requirements document or start the interview. It joins the interview (<a href="screens/05-interview-running.html">05</a>) or the documents (<a href="screens/08-documents.html">08</a>) and the founder journey continues.</li>
        </ol></div>
      <div class="ss-card"><h3 class="pm-t-heading">Lane B, step by step</h3>
        <ol class="ss-list">
          <li><a href="screens/21-repo-connect.html">21</a> choose a repository and read the GitHub App check. <a href="screens/21b-repo-connect-permission.html">21b</a> the App is not installed; <a href="screens/21c-repo-connect-empty.html">21c</a> no repositories found.</li>
          <li><a href="screens/22-repo-requests.html">22</a> the request loop: a composer and the requests in rank order with fixed pins. <a href="screens/22b-repo-requests-empty.html">22b</a> no requests yet.</li>
          <li><a href="screens/23-repo-request.html">23</a> one request, ready to merge, with its four-step tape (Build, Test, Review, Merge). <a href="screens/23b-repo-request-blocked.html">23b</a> a check did not pass.</li>
          <li>A Lane B project has no interview, documents or roadmap in this proposal (an open question below): its rail is Requests, Settings and Live logs.</li>
        </ol></div>
    </div>
    <p class="ss-lede">Vocabulary (Ruling 14). Founder screens keep the plain words: "repository" appears only inside a live safeguard sentence quoted verbatim, and "clone" and "PRD" never appear ("requirements document" replaces PRD). Lane B screens may say repository, pull request, branch, merge and deploy; branch names and pull request numbers sit in a row's meta line, in mono, never inside a pin sentence. Commit ids, job ids and digests stay under Details on every lane. Thumbnails of all fourteen lane screens are in <a href="#screens">All 34 screens</a>.</p>

    <div>
      <h3 class="pm-t-heading">Four trend items, adapted</h3>
      <p class="ss-lede">Each comes from trend research and is adapted to fit the laws: none may add a second thread, hide a fact, or move without a state change.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pm-table-scroll"><table class="pm-table ss-plain ss-wide"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">How it is adapted here</th><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">Component</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>T-1 Dictation</strong></td><td>Voice in the composer. A ghost mic button writes into the text box; the text is checked and sent by the person, never by voice. It falls back to a stated unavailable state.</td><td><a href="screens/05-interview-running.html">05</a>, <a href="screens/05b-interview-empty.html">05b</a>, <a href="screens/06-interview-finished.html">06</a>, <a href="screens/20-handoff-requirements.html">20</a>, <a href="screens/22-repo-requests.html">22</a>, <a href="screens/22b-repo-requests-empty.html">22b</a></td><td><a href="#n-dictate">Dictation</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>T-2 One autonomy setting</strong></td><td>One plain switch, "Check with me before each sprint starts", with its consequence as a sentence. No permission matrix, no "always allow".</td><td><a href="screens/16-settings.html">16</a>, with consequence lines on <a href="screens/11-roadmap-awaiting.html">11</a> and <a href="screens/13-sprints-building.html">13</a></td><td><a href="#n-setting">Setting switch</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>T-3 Bento overview</strong></td><td>Importance-sized tiles in reading order. The lead tile is the decision and keeps the one thread; every digit keeps its sentence. Not used on lists or boards.</td><td><a href="screens/03-overview-decision.html">03</a>, <a href="screens/04-overview-paused.html">04</a>, <a href="screens/19-handoff-copying.html">19</a></td><td><a href="#n-bento">Bento tiles</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>T-4 Quiet milestone</strong></td><td>The tape's checks stitch shut once when a sprint is ready or all sprints are accepted, with one line. No confetti, no sound, reduced motion respected.</td><td><a href="screens/13-sprints-building.html">13</a> (ready state), <a href="screens/14-sprints-accepted.html">14</a>, <a href="flow.html">flow</a></td><td><a href="#n-milestone">Quiet milestone</a></td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 6. Status vocabulary -->
<section class="ss-sec" id="status" aria-labelledby="h-status">
  <header class="pm-section-head pm-section-head--page ss-head"><h2 id="h-status">Status words</h2><span class="pm-meta">SPEC D.5 and E</span></header>
  <div class="ss-body">
    <p class="ss-lede">Seven pins, fixed labels, each followed by one plain sentence. Wire words appear verbatim as facts inside the sentence or under Details. Anything else is a bug.</p>
    <div class="pm-table-scroll"><table class="pm-table ss-plain ss-wide"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Pin</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th><th scope="col">The sentence rule</th><th scope="col">Real sentence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="needs-you"><span class="pm-pin-head"></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Needs you</span></span></td><td>You must act.</td><td>Starts with the verb.</td><td>Answer the next interview question.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="working" data-live="true"><span class="pm-pin-head"></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Working</span></span></td><td>Pramaan is doing something.</td><td>Pramaan is a gerund. Nothing needed from you.</td><td>Pramaan is building sprint 1 (building). Nothing needed from you.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="waiting"><span class="pm-pin-head"></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Waiting</span></span></td><td>Queued behind something else.</td><td>Starts after the thing.</td><td>Starts after sprint 1 is accepted.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="done"><span class="pm-pin-head"><svg class="pm-pin-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pm-g-check"/></svg></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Done</span></span></td><td>Finished and, where it applies, accepted.</td><td>Who accepted it and when.</td><td>Accepted by you Tuesday 14:10.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="paused"><span class="pm-pin-head"><svg class="pm-pin-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pm-g-bar"/></svg></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Paused</span></span></td><td>Stopped on purpose, can resume.</td><td>The reason, then how to resume.</td><td>Paused because the monthly budget is used up. Raise it in Settings to continue.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="blocked"><span class="pm-pin-head"><svg class="pm-pin-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pm-g-x"/></svg></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Blocked</span></span></td><td>Cannot continue without a fix.</td><td>What failed, then what to try.</td><td>A check did not pass. Pramaan is fixing it; nothing needed from you.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="locked"><span class="pm-pin-head"><svg class="pm-pin-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pm-g-lock"/></svg></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Locked</span></span></td><td>Read only for now.</td><td>Why, then what you can do instead.</td><td>Read only while sprint 1 is being built. Open Build to see progress.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <div class="ss-grid2">
      <div><h3 class="pm-t-heading">From today's phrasings</h3>
        <table class="pm-table ss-plain"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Today</th><th scope="col">Pin</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>Building</td><td>Working</td></tr><tr><td>Drafting documents</td><td>Working</td></tr><tr><td>Paused</td><td>Paused, with the reason</td></tr><tr><td>In the interview</td><td>Needs you</td></tr><tr><td>Plan approved</td><td>Working if a sprint runs, else Waiting</td></tr><tr><td>All planned sprints accepted</td><td>Done</td></tr><tr><td>Waiting for the next draft (footer)</td><td>Working, folded into the sentence</td></tr><tr><td>Dependency monitoring paused (footer)</td><td>No pin: a setting, shown only in Settings</td></tr><tr><td>accepted / draft (documents)</td><td>Done / Needs you</td></tr><tr><td>In progress / Planned / Accepted / Not started</td><td>Working / Waiting / Done / Waiting</td></tr><tr><td>Plan being drafted / awaiting approval / approved</td><td>Working / Needs you / Done</td></tr><tr><td>Ready to try</td><td>Needs you</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
      <div><h3 class="pm-t-heading">From wire states</h3>
        <table class="pm-table ss-plain"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Wire</th><th scope="col">Pin</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="pm-mono">intake, classifying, provisioning, defining, designing, building, validating</span></td><td>Working</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="pm-mono">awaiting_acceptance</span></td><td>Needs you</td></tr><tr><td><span class="pm-mono">accepted</span></td><td>Done</td></tr><tr><td><span class="pm-mono">blocked</span></td><td>Blocked</td></tr><tr><td><span class="pm-mono">archived</span></td><td>Locked: "Archived. Restore it from Settings."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Asset <span class="pm-mono">generating</span></td><td>Working</td></tr><tr><td>Asset <span class="pm-mono">draft, pending</span></td><td>Needs you</td></tr><tr><td>Asset <span class="pm-mono">accepted</span></td><td>Done</td></tr><tr><td>Asset <span class="pm-mono">stale</span></td><td>Waiting for a fresh draft after the brief changed</td></tr><tr><td>Asset <span class="pm-mono">rejected</span></td><td>Waiting: "You asked for changes. A new draft is coming."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Job <span class="pm-mono">running / queued / done / failed / cancelled</span></td><td>Working / Waiting / Done / Blocked / Paused</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Next action <span class="pm-mono">connect_repository, confirm_classification, review_asset, accept_set, start_sprint, resolve_blocker</span></td><td>Needs you, with a verb sentence</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Anything unknown</td><td>No pin. Never guess.</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="pm-t-heading">Requests (Lane B)</h3>
      <p class="ss-lede">A request moves through the same seven pins. The mapping from the wire feature states is fixed (D-P2-5). "Waiting for review" is not a label: there are seven, and it is a Working sentence.</p>
      <div class="pm-table-scroll"><table class="pm-table ss-plain ss-wide"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Wire state</th><th scope="col">Pin</th><th scope="col">Sentence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="pm-mono">planned</span></td><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="waiting"><span class="pm-pin-head"></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Waiting</span></span></td><td>Starts after 'Send a summary email every Monday'.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pm-mono">implementing, verifying, reviewing, publishing</span></td><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="working" data-live="true"><span class="pm-pin-head"></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Working</span></span></td><td>The sentence names the stage.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pm-mono">pr_open</span>, review pending</td><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="working" data-live="true"><span class="pm-pin-head"></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Working</span></span></td><td>The review is running, round n.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pm-mono">pr_open</span>, ready</td><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="needs-you"><span class="pm-pin-head"></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Needs you</span></span></td><td>Reviewed twice and ready. Merge it when you are ready.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pm-mono">merged</span></td><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="done"><span class="pm-pin-head"><svg class="pm-pin-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pm-g-check"/></svg></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Done</span></span></td><td>Merged by you Tuesday 14:10.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pm-mono">blocked, failed</span></td><td><span class="pm-pin" data-status="blocked"><span class="pm-pin-head"><svg class="pm-pin-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pm-g-x"/></svg></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Blocked</span></span></td><td>A check did not pass. Pramaan is fixing it; nothing needed from you.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="pm-t-heading">Copy rules</h3>
      <ul class="ss-list ss-copy"><li>Sentences under 14 words. Literal verbs, second person, present tense.</li><li>No jargon: token, digest, repo, PRD, UAT and deploy become budget, details, code, product brief, try it and go live.</li><li>Wire words only verbatim, inside a sentence or under Details. Numbers as digits.</li><li>No em dash (use a full stop or a comma), no exclamation marks, no "Oops", no "AI-powered".</li><li>Pramaan is the actor. "Your product partner" appears only in the interview header.</li><li>Founder screens never say clone or PRD, and say repository only inside a quoted safeguard sentence. Lane B screens may say repository, pull request, branch and merge.</li></ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="pm-t-heading">Microcopy</h3>
      <div class="pm-table-scroll"><table class="pm-table ss-plain"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Place</th><th scope="col">Copy</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<!--MICROCOPY-->
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

