<!-- 7b. Decisions and open questions (SPEC P.6) -->
<section class="ss-sec" id="decisions" aria-labelledby="h-decisions">
  <header class="pm-section-head pm-section-head--page ss-head"><h2 id="h-decisions">Decisions and open questions</h2><span class="pm-meta">SPEC P.6</span></header>
  <div class="ss-body">
    <p class="ss-lede">Where the live build speaks, the design follows it. Where the sources conflict, the choice is recorded and flagged. The CPO has ruled on four (decided and closed); the rest are recorded or still open for the CEO.</p>
    <div>
      <h3 class="pm-t-heading">CPO rulings, 2026-10-01 (decided, closed)</h3>
      <div class="pm-table-scroll"><table class="pm-table ss-plain ss-wide"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Ruling</th><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Decision</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">R1</td><td>D-P2-1: where the private copy lives.</td><td>The private copy follows the live build: "a private repository Pramaan holds".</td><td><span class="ss-ok">Decided</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">R2</td><td>D-P2-2: the write rules of the two lanes.</td><td>They follow the live build's behaviour and wording. Lane A never writes back to the source. Lane B opens pull requests in the user's repository and never pushes to the default branch.</td><td><span class="ss-ok">Decided</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">R3</td><td>Q2: the .zip upload.</td><td>Kept exactly as the live build states it: a 200 MB .zip, 1 GB and 50,000 files unpacked. No further verification needed.</td><td><span class="ss-ok">Decided</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">R4</td><td>Ruling 7: the icon-only collapsed rail as the default below 1280px.</td><td>Accepted as designed, with the permanent expand button and the one-time hint kept.</td><td><span class="ss-ok">Decided</span></td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="pm-t-heading">Recorded decisions</h3>
      <div class="pm-table-scroll"><table class="pm-table ss-plain ss-wide"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Id</th><th scope="col">Decision</th><th scope="col">State</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">D-P2-1</td><td>The private copy is a private repository Pramaan holds; founder words on screen, the literal fact under Details. (Backend decision D6 says repositories are customer-owned; the design states the live build's version.)</td><td><span class="ss-ok">Decided</span> (R1)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">D-P2-2</td><td>Opposite write rules, stated verbatim on their screens and never mixed. The lane is chosen on the projects list and can be switched only before a project exists. Moving a project from A to B is not designed.</td><td><span class="ss-ok">Decided</span> (R2)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">D-P2-3</td><td>"Take a copy" downloads a .zip. "Export to GitHub is not available yet." stays the Waiting sentence. The live sentence about exporting a copy to GitHub is not quoted, because its second half contradicts Settings.</td><td>Recorded. <strong>CEO: is the .zip download real today?</strong> If not, the button becomes a Waiting sentence too.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">D-P2-4</td><td>Lane B has its own home (Requests), its own rail (Requests, Settings, Live logs) and a per-request measure instead of the five-step tape. Inferred, not observed.</td><td>Open. <strong>CEO: does a Lane B project also get documents and a roadmap, or only requests?</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">D-P2-5</td><td>The request status vocabulary maps the wire feature states to the seven pins (see Status words).</td><td>Recorded.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">D-P2-6</td><td>Merging happens on GitHub. The thread on a ready request is "Open pull request #42". Auto-merge is a Lane B setting, default off.</td><td>Recorded. <strong>CEO: confirm there is no in-app merge button.</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">D-P2-7</td><td>A requirements document brought on screen 20 becomes "Requirements, Draft 1, imported by you" and is Needs you until the founder accepts it. The interview step then reads done and still opens.</td><td>Recorded.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">D-P2-8</td><td>The product idea is the first decision on every idea-lane project.</td><td>Recorded.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="pm-mono">D-P2-9</td><td>GitHub permission wording: the screen says what Pramaan does ("reads your code once and never changes it") and that GitHub shows what it asks for. It does not promise a read-only permission.</td><td>Recorded. <strong>CEO: confirm once the GitHub App unification lands.</strong></td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="pm-t-heading">Still open, for the CEO</h3>
      <p class="ss-lede">Questions the design cannot decide.</p>
      <ul class="ss-list">
        <li><span class="pm-mono">D-P2-4</span> Does a Lane B project get an interview, documents and a roadmap, or only requests?</li>
        <li><span class="pm-mono">D-P2-3, D-P2-6, D-P2-9</span> The three confirmations above: the .zip download, no in-app merge button, the GitHub permission wording.</li>
        <li><span class="pm-mono">Q6</span> Who "reviewed" a pull request: the review agent, the PR bot or both, and is the verdict shown to the user. The design shows "Round 1 asked for ..., Round 2 passed." as plain lines.</li>
        <li><span class="pm-mono">Q8</span> Deployment: Lane B says "you deploy" and nothing in the app shows it; the design states it under "What stays with you" only.</li>
        <li><span class="pm-mono">Q9</span> What the copy step reads from the code and how long it takes (screen 19 shows three steps, no durations).</li>
        <li><span class="pm-mono">Q10</span> Is dependency monitoring on by default for Lane A and B projects (screen 16 shows it off for todo).</li>
        <li><span class="pm-mono">Q11</span> Errors not designed: install revoked mid-run, branch protection blocking the pull request, a pull request closed unmerged, merge conflicts, a Lane B baseline that already fails.</li>
        <li><span class="pm-mono">Q13</span> Branch choice, multiple repositories, monorepo subfolders and forks in the pickers (none offered).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 8. Three moves -->
<section class="ss-sec" id="moves" aria-labelledby="h-moves">
  <header class="pm-section-head pm-section-head--page ss-head"><h2 id="h-moves">The three out-of-the-box moves</h2><span class="pm-meta">SPEC G</span></header>
  <div class="ss-body">
    <article class="ss-comp" id="m-tape" aria-labelledby="h-m-tape">
      <div class="ss-comp-head"><h3 id="h-m-tape">1. The live tape: where you are, measured</h3><span class="pm-meta">G.1</span></div>
      <p class="ss-lede">The tape is not a stepper, it is a measure. Sub-progress ticks show how far a step is, the pin sits on the real stage, and the shank reaches down into the decision below. On the overview it is printed large, the only place it grows. Move the project through its stages and watch the pin slide.</p>
      <div class="ss-stage"><div class="ss-tapebox"><div class="ss-tape" id="m-tape-live" data-large="1"></div></div>
        <div class="ss-stepper" role="group" aria-label="Move the project to a stage"><span class="ss-cap">Project stage:</span><button class="pm-btn pm-btn--quiet pm-btn--sm" type="button" data-stage="0" aria-pressed="false">Interview</button><button class="pm-btn pm-btn--quiet pm-btn--sm" type="button" data-stage="1" aria-pressed="true">Documents</button><button class="pm-btn pm-btn--quiet pm-btn--sm" type="button" data-stage="2" aria-pressed="false">Roadmap</button><button class="pm-btn pm-btn--quiet pm-btn--sm" type="button" data-stage="3" aria-pressed="false">Build</button><button class="pm-btn pm-btn--quiet pm-btn--sm" type="button" data-stage="4" aria-pressed="false">Try it</button></div></div>
    </article>
    <article class="ss-comp" id="m-strip" aria-labelledby="h-m-strip">
      <div class="ss-comp-head"><h3 id="h-m-strip">2. The Nothing-is-lost strip</h3><span class="pm-meta">G.2</span></div>
      <p class="ss-lede">A 28px strip under the top bar answers the founder's real fear: did my work disappear when I closed the tab? It only states facts the system already has. Open History for the last eight saves and acceptances.</p>
      <div class="ss-stage"><div class="ss-strip-demo"><div class="pm-strip"><span class="pm-strip-text" id="m-strip-text">Last saved: your decision "First turn", <time datetime="2026-09-30T14:10">14:10</time> &middot; Last accepted: Product brief draft 1, <time datetime="2026-09-29">Tuesday</time></span><button class="pm-strip-history" type="button" popovertarget="pm-history">History</button></div></div>
        <div class="ss-row"><button class="pm-btn pm-btn--ghost pm-btn--sm" type="button" id="m-strip-save">Demo: save a decision</button><span class="ss-cap">An empty project reads: "Nothing saved yet. Your first answer is kept the moment you send it."</span></div></div>
      <div class="pm-history" id="pm-history" popover aria-label="Recently saved or accepted"><ol>
        <li><time datetime="2026-09-30T14:10">14:10</time><span>Saved decision "First turn"</span><a href="screens/05-interview-running.html">Open</a></li><li><time datetime="2026-09-30T14:08">14:08</time><span>Saved decision "End of game"</span><a href="screens/05-interview-running.html">Open</a></li><li><time datetime="2026-09-30T14:05">14:05</time><span>Saved decision "Who plays"</span><a href="screens/05-interview-running.html">Open</a></li><li><time datetime="2026-09-29">Tuesday</time><span>Accepted Product brief, draft 1</span><a href="screens/10-document-locked.html">Open</a></li>
        <li><time datetime="2026-09-29">Tuesday</time><span>Accepted Requirements, draft 1</span><a href="screens/08-documents.html">Open</a></li><li><time datetime="2026-09-29">Tuesday</time><span>Accepted User journey, draft 1</span><a href="screens/08-documents.html">Open</a></li><li><time datetime="2026-09-29">Tuesday</time><span>Saved decision "Start over early"</span><a href="screens/05-interview-running.html">Open</a></li><li><time datetime="2026-09-29">Tuesday</time><span>Saved decision "Product idea"</span><a href="screens/05-interview-running.html">Open</a></li></ol></div>
    </article>
    <article class="ss-comp" id="m-words" aria-labelledby="h-m-words">
      <div class="ss-comp-head"><h3 id="h-m-words">3. Your words on the plan</h3><span class="pm-meta">G.3</span></div>
      <p class="ss-lede">One switch puts your own interview sentences beside every outcome and every check. You judge the plan, and later the product, against what you said. The switch is page wide here, so the route and checklist samples above show their quotes too.</p>
      <div class="ss-stage">
        <div class="ss-words"><input class="pm-switch" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="m-words-switch" data-words-toggle aria-describedby="m-words-note"><label class="pm-label" for="m-words-switch">Show my words</label><span class="ss-cap" id="m-words-note">Quotes come only from decisions you saved.</span></div>
        <ol class="pm-route" aria-label="Sprint 1 with your words"><li class="pm-route-node" data-status="waiting"><span class="pm-route-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="pm-route-card"><div class="pm-route-title"><h4>Sprint 1 · Your private checklist</h4><span class="pm-pin" data-status="waiting"><span class="pm-pin-head"></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Waiting</span><span class="pm-pin-sentence">Starts after you approve the plan.</span></span></div><p class="pm-route-label">You will be able to:</p><ul class="pm-route-outcomes"><li>Sign up with an email and password<span class="pm-said">You said: 'users can sign up or log in and see only their own tasks' <a class="pm-said-edit" href="screens/05-interview-running.html">Edit that decision</a></span></li><li>Log in with the right password and see your empty checklist</li><li>Add a third task and see it appear at the bottom, below the first two</li></ul></div></li></ol>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 9. Non-goals and risks -->
<section class="ss-sec" id="risks" aria-labelledby="h-risks">
  <header class="pm-section-head pm-section-head--page ss-head"><h2 id="h-risks">Risks and limits</h2><span class="pm-meta">SPEC H</span></header>
  <div class="ss-body">
    <p class="ss-lede"><strong>Not in this system:</strong> mobile and tablet layouts (below 1024px the rail collapses and panels stack, nothing more), the marketing site, the dependency monitoring view beyond its Settings entry, an icon style beyond the 1.5px stroke set, live data (every screen is static), and any change to route structure or the wire vocabulary. Pass 2 also leaves undrawn a Lane B interview, documents and roadmap (open question D-P2-4) and the Lane B settings screen (specified, not drawn).</p>
    <div class="pm-table-scroll"><table class="pm-table ss-plain ss-wide"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Risk</th><th scope="col">Guard</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>The canary reads as a warning colour.</td><td>The thread is always a filled button with ink text and an ink border, never a stripe, ring or tint. Paused is clay, never yellow. There is no other amber.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>The tailor's world tips into costume.</td><td>Each carrier has one job in one place: stitch for seams, pin for status and you-are-here, chalk for annotation and the active marker, tape for journey and progress. No textures, no fabric, no tailoring words in copy.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ink rail plus a light page looks heavy at 1142.</td><td>Below 1280px the default rail is the 64px icon rail on every screen, one state for the whole app (Ruling 7, accepted by the CPO as R4). Wordmark and icons are flat ink-100 on ink-900.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>One family for everything feels flat.</td><td>Reading 17/28 against Body 15/22 gives documents and chat their own voice. Engraved digits carry the only display moments.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>The strip and the large tape cost vertical space.</td><td>The strip is 28px on project screens only. The large tape exists only on the overview, where the decision still starts by y = 204.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>The verdict checklist adds three buttons per item.</td><td>28px quiet toggles, keys 1, 2, 3 inside an item, and a panel wide enough for one row.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>The auto-collapsed rail feels like lost navigation.</td><td>Collapsed keeps icons, tooltips, the pen circle, the project tile and a permanent expand button, with a one-time hint. Your explicit expand is remembered.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Chalk marks lose contrast on grey.</td><td>Chalk text is only ever on chalk tint or raised (7.07:1 and 8.40:1). Chalk on the sunken surface is unchecked and forbidden.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Two thread copies at once (top bar and action bar).</td><td>An observer hides one. The check counts visible <span class="pm-mono">[data-thread]</span> and fails on 2.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Dark theme is secondary.</td><td>Every pair in the contrast table is verified for dark. Documents default to light. Dark is a toggle, remembered in <span class="pm-mono">pm.theme</span>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pass 2: a fitted panel makes the column under it look unfinished.</td><td>The panel is sticky on page screens, so it stays in view while the main job scrolls. Its content states facts the founder wants at hand: plan at a glance, this project. The tool exempts only the column under it, never a hole beside the main job.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pass 2: the bento reads as a dashboard.</td><td>One lead tile holds the one thread. The digits keep their sentences. Tiles are sized by importance in DOM order. No sparkline, no percentage besides the budget, no tile without a sentence.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pass 2: two audiences drift into two products.</td><td>The shell, pins, buttons and tape anatomy are identical on Lane B. Only the words change (Ruling 14), and the same seven pins carry request states.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </div>
</section>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>

<div class="pm-popover" id="c-pop2" popover data-anchor="invoker" aria-label="Comment on this passage"><p class="pm-label">Comment on this passage</p><p class="pm-muted" style="margin-top:4px">Your comments are sent together when you ask for changes.</p></div>
<dialog class="pm-dialog" id="c-dlg" aria-labelledby="c-dlg-t"><h2 class="pm-dialog-title" id="c-dlg-t">Stop this sprint?</h2><p class="pm-dialog-text">Pramaan stops building now. Work that already passed its checks stays saved.</p><div class="pm-dialog-actions"><button class="pm-btn pm-btn--quiet" type="button" data-close>Keep going</button><button class="pm-btn pm-btn--danger" type="button" data-close>Stop the sprint</button></div></dialog>
<div class="pm-toast-host" id="c-toast-host"></div>

<script>
(function () {
  "use strict";
  var root = document.documentElement;
  var $ = function (s, r) { return (r || document).querySelector(s); };
  var $$ = function (s, r) { return Array.prototype.slice.call((r || document).querySelectorAll(s)); };
  var ICON = function (id, cls) { return '<svg class="pm-i ' + cls + '"><use href="#' + id + '"/></svg>'; };

  /* 1. Tapes: built from data-tape="state[:done/total],..." with the shipped markup, before shell.js positions the pin. */
  var LABELS = ["Interview", "Documents", "Roadmap", "Build", "Try it"];
  function tapeStep(i, spec) {
    var p = spec.split(":"), state = p[0], prog = p[1] ? p[1].split("/") : null, n = i + 1, L = LABELS[i], sr = '<span class="pm-sr">Step ' + n + ', </span>';
    if (state === "locked") return '<li data-state="locked"><span class="pm-tape-step" aria-disabled="true" title="Opens after the plan is approved"><span class="pm-tape-label">' + sr + L + '<span class="pm-sr">, locked. Opens after the plan is approved</span></span><span class="pm-tape-num" aria-hidden="true">' + ICON("i-lock", "pm-i--12") + '</span></span></li>';
    var num = state === "done" ? ICON("i-check", "pm-i--12") : n, ticks = "", note = state === "done" ? ", done" : state === "current" ? ". You are here" : ", not started";
    if (prog) { ticks = '<span class="pm-tape-ticks" aria-hidden="true">'; for (var k = 0; k < +prog[1]; k++) ticks += '<i' + (k < +prog[0] ? ' class="on"' : "") + '></i>'; ticks += "</span>"; note = ", " + prog[0] + " of " + prog[1] + (state === "current" ? ". You are here" : ""); }
    return '<li data-state="' + state + '"' + (prog ? ' data-progress="' + prog.join("/") + '"' : "") + '><a class="pm-tape-step" href="#c-tape"' + (state === "current" ? ' aria-current="step"' : "") + '><span class="pm-tape-label">' + sr + L + '<span class="pm-sr">' + note + '</span></span><span class="pm-tape-num pm-tnum" aria-hidden="true">' + num + "</span>" + ticks + "</a></li>";
  }
  function tapeHTML(list, large) { return '<nav class="pm-tape' + (large ? " pm-tape--large" : "") + '" aria-label="Your journey"><ol>' + list.map(function (s, i) { return tapeStep(i, s); }).join("") + '</ol><span class="pm-tape-pin" aria-hidden="true"></span></nav>'; }
  $$(".ss-tape[data-tape]").forEach(function (el) { el.innerHTML = tapeHTML(el.getAttribute("data-tape").split(","), false); });
  var live = $("#m-tape-live"), PROG = ["3/6", "2/3", "", "1/3", ""];
  function stageSpec(i) { return LABELS.map(function (_, k) { var s = k < i ? "done" : k === i ? "current" : (k === 4 && i < 3 ? "locked" : "upcoming"); return k === i && PROG[k] ? s + ":" + PROG[k] : s; }); }
  live.innerHTML = tapeHTML(stageSpec(1), true);
  $$("[data-stage]").forEach(function (b) {
    b.addEventListener("click", function () {
      var i = +b.getAttribute("data-stage"), spec = stageSpec(i), lis = $$("li", live);
      /* Replace each step's content, then flip data-state: shell.js watches data-state and slides the pin in 240ms. */
      lis.forEach(function (li, k) { var t = document.createElement("div"); t.innerHTML = tapeStep(k, spec[k]); var n = t.firstChild; li.innerHTML = n.innerHTML; if (n.hasAttribute("data-progress")) li.setAttribute("data-progress", n.getAttribute("data-progress")); else li.removeAttribute("data-progress"); li.setAttribute("data-state", n.getAttribute("data-state")); });
      $$("[data-stage]").forEach(function (o) { o.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(o === b)); });
    });
  });

  /* 2. Colour tokens, read live. Hex comes from a canvas so it is the true sRGB twin of the OKLCH value. */
  var REF = { ink: [950, 900, 800, 700, 600, 500, 400, 300, 200, 100, 50, 0], thread: [500, 600, 700, 800], chalk: [700, 600, 400, 300, 100, 50], moss: [600, 400, 100, 900], clay: [600, 400, 100, 900], red: [600, 400, 100, 900] };
  var SYS = "ground surface-raised surface-sunken surface-rail surface-rail-active text text-secondary text-muted text-meta text-on-rail text-on-rail-muted text-on-ink hairline hairline-on-rail control-border thread thread-hover thread-text thread-text-hover on-thread chalk chalk-text chalk-tint chalk-on-rail status-needs-you status-needs-you-tint status-working status-working-tint status-waiting status-waiting-tint status-done status-done-tint status-paused status-paused-tint status-blocked status-blocked-tint status-locked status-locked-tint focus focus-halo focus-on-rail selection-bg selection-text scrim".split(" ").map(function (n) { return "--pm-sys-" + n; });
  var cx = document.createElement("canvas").getContext("2d", { willReadFrequently: true });
  cx.canvas.width = cx.canvas.height = 1;
  function hexOf(v) { cx.clearRect(0, 0, 1, 1); cx.fillStyle = "#000000"; cx.fillStyle = v; cx.fillRect(0, 0, 1, 1); var d = cx.getImageData(0, 0, 1, 1).data; return d[3] < 255 ? "alpha " + Math.round(d[3] / 2.55) + "%" : "#" + [d[0], d[1], d[2]].map(function (n) { return n.toString(16).padStart(2, "0"); }).join(""); }
  var cs0 = getComputedStyle(root), html = "";
  Object.keys(REF).forEach(function (f) {
    html += '<div class="ss-family"><h3>' + f + '</h3><ul class="ss-swatches">' + REF[f].map(function (w) {
      var n = "--pm-ref-" + f + "-" + w, v = cs0.getPropertyValue(n).trim();
      return '<li class="ss-sw"><i class="ss-chip" style="background:var(' + n + ')"></i><span class="ss-sw-text"><span class="pm-t-label">' + f + "-" + w + '</span><span class="pm-mono">' + hexOf(v) + '</span><span class="pm-mono">' + v + "</span></span></li>";
    }).join("") + "</ul></div>";
  });
  $("#ss-ref").innerHTML = html;
  function grab(theme) {
    var prev = root.getAttribute("data-theme"), o = {};
    root.classList.add("pm-no-anim"); root.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
    var cs = getComputedStyle(root); SYS.forEach(function (n) { o[n] = cs.getPropertyValue(n).trim(); });
    if (prev === null) root.removeAttribute("data-theme"); else root.setAttribute("data-theme", prev);
    cs.getPropertyValue("--pm-sys-text"); root.classList.remove("pm-no-anim");
    return o;
  }
  var L = grab("light"), D = grab("dark"), rows = "";
  function cell(v) { return '<span class="ss-role"><i class="ss-chip" style="background:' + v + '"></i><span class="pm-mono">' + hexOf(v) + "</span></span>"; }
  SYS.forEach(function (n) { rows += '<tr><td class="pm-mono">' + n + "</td><td>" + cell(L[n]) + "</td><td>" + cell(D[n]) + "</td></tr>"; });
  $("#ss-roles tbody").innerHTML = rows;

  /* 3. Theme and density toggles, contents scroll-spy, live demos. */
  function boot() {
    var tb = $("#ss-theme"), db = $("#ss-density"), main = $("#pm-main");
    function paintTheme() { var d = window.pmTheme() === "dark"; tb.textContent = d ? "Light theme" : "Dark theme"; tb.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(d)); }
    tb.addEventListener("click", function () { window.pmTheme("toggle"); });
    root.addEventListener("pm:theme", paintTheme); paintTheme();
    db.addEventListener("click", function () {
      var on = db.getAttribute("aria-pressed") !== "true";
      $$("[data-density-target]").forEach(function (el) { if (on) el.setAttribute("data-density", "compact"); else el.removeAttribute("data-density"); });
      db.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(on)); db.textContent = on ? "Comfortable rows" : "Compact rows";
    });
    /* The style guide reads best with the rail collapsed; a saved choice to keep it open wins. */
    var saved = null; try { saved = localStorage.getItem("pm.rail"); } catch (e) {}
    if (window.pmShell && saved !== "expanded") window.pmShell.setRail("collapsed");
    /* The rail item samples are inert: keep the real rail as the keyboard tab stop. */
    $$(".ss-inkbox .pm-rail-item").forEach(function (a) { a.setAttribute("tabindex", "-1"); });
    var first = $(".pm-rail .pm-rail-item"); if (first) first.setAttribute("tabindex", "0");
    /* Contents rail follows the scroll. */
    var links = $$(".ss-layout > .pm-toc ol a"), secs = links.map(function (a) { return $(a.getAttribute("href")); }), q = false;
    function spy() { q = false; var line = main.getBoundingClientRect().top + 130, cur = 0; secs.forEach(function (s, i) { if (s.getBoundingClientRect().top <= line) cur = i; }); if (main.scrollTop + main.clientHeight >= main.scrollHeight - 2) cur = secs.length - 1; links.forEach(function (a, i) { if (i === cur) a.setAttribute("aria-current", "location"); else a.removeAttribute("aria-current"); }); }
    main.addEventListener("scroll", function () { if (!q) { q = true; requestAnimationFrame(spy); } }, { passive: true }); spy();
    /* Form save demo */
    var nameEl = $("#c-name"), save = $("#c-save-btn"), reason = $("#c-save-reason"), saved2 = $("#c-saved");
    nameEl.addEventListener("input", function () { var ch = nameEl.value !== "todo"; saved2.hidden = true; save.setAttribute("aria-disabled", ch ? "false" : "true"); reason.hidden = ch; });
    save.addEventListener("click", function () { if (save.getAttribute("aria-disabled") === "true") return; save.setAttribute("aria-disabled", "true"); reason.hidden = true; saved2.hidden = false; });
    $$(".pm-chip").forEach(function (c) { c.addEventListener("click", function () { if (c.getAttribute("aria-disabled") === "true") return; if (c.getAttribute("role") === "radio") return; c.setAttribute("aria-checked", c.getAttribute("aria-checked") === "true" ? "false" : "true"); }); });
    /* Milestone sample: pmMilestone plays on the first visible tape in the document and this page has many, so the sample's own tape is the only one visible for the synchronous call. */
    var msBox = $("#n-milestone");
    document.addEventListener("click", function (e) {
      var b = e.target.closest && e.target.closest("#n-milestone [data-milestone-trigger]");
      if (!b || !window.pmMilestone) return;
      e.stopPropagation();
      var others = $$(".pm-tape").filter(function (t) { return !msBox.contains(t); }), was = others.map(function (t) { return t.hidden; });
      others.forEach(function (t) { t.hidden = true; });
      window.pmMilestone(b.getAttribute("data-milestone-trigger") || "sprint-ready");
      others.forEach(function (t, i) { t.hidden = was[i]; });
    }, true);
    /* Dialog and toast */
    var dlg = $("#c-dlg"); $("#c-dlg-btn").addEventListener("click", function () { dlg.showModal(); });
    dlg.addEventListener("click", function (e) { if (e.target.hasAttribute("data-close")) dlg.close(); });
    $("#c-toast-btn").addEventListener("click", function () {
      var host = $("#c-toast-host"), t = document.createElement("div"), timer;
      t.className = "pm-toast"; t.setAttribute("role", "status"); t.dataset.state = "enter";
      t.innerHTML = '<span class="pm-pin" data-status="done"><span class="pm-pin-head"><svg class="pm-pin-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pm-g-check"/></svg></span><span class="pm-pin-label">Done</span></span><span>Draft 1 accepted. The plan opens next.</span>';
      function leave() { t.dataset.state = "leave"; setTimeout(function () { t.remove(); }, 90); }
      function arm() { timer = setTimeout(leave, 6000); }
      t.addEventListener("mouseenter", function () { clearTimeout(timer); }); t.addEventListener("mouseleave", arm);
      host.appendChild(t); arm();
    });
    /* Strip demo: a save updates Last saved and the History list */
    $("#m-strip-save").addEventListener("click", function () {
      var d = new Date(), hm = ("0" + d.getHours()).slice(-2) + ":" + ("0" + d.getMinutes()).slice(-2), t = $("#m-strip-text");
      var acc = t.innerHTML.split("&middot;")[1] || t.innerHTML.split("·")[1] || "";
      t.innerHTML = 'Last saved: your decision "Start over early", <time datetime="' + d.toISOString() + '">' + hm + "</time> &middot;" + acc;
      var ol = $("#pm-history ol"), li = document.createElement("li"); li.innerHTML = '<time datetime="' + d.toISOString() + '">' + hm + '</time><span>Saved decision "Start over early"</span><a href="screens/05-interview-running.html">Open</a>'; ol.insertBefore(li, ol.firstChild); if (ol.children.length > 8) ol.lastChild.remove();
    });
  }
  if (document.readyState === "loading") document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", boot); else boot();
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
